{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CxGNmYdpMevdNX3ZdEZC9q","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# mod10_counter\n2\t\n3\tA 4-bit BCD (mod-10) up counter with synchronous load, count enable, and a carry-out.\n4\t\n5\t## Ports\n6\t| Port  | Dir | Width | Description |\n7\t|-------|-----|-------|-------------|\n8\t| clk   | in  | 1     | Rising-edge clock |\n9\t| rst_n | in  | 1     | Asynchronous active-low reset |\n10\t| en    | in  | 1     | Count enable |\n11\t| load  | in  | 1     | Synchronous load (has priority over `en`) |\n12\t| d     | in  | 4     | Load value |\n13\t| q     | out | 4     | Current count, 0..9 (registered) |\n14\t| co    | out | 1     | Carry-out (combinational) |\n15\t\n16\t## Behavior\n17\t- While `rst_n` is low, `q` is 0.\n18\t- On a rising edge of `clk` with `load` high, `q` takes `d`. If `d` is greater than 9 (not a\n19\t  valid BCD digit), `q` takes 0 instead. `load` works regardless of `en`.\n20\t- Otherwise, on a rising edge with `en` high, `q` increments by 1, wrapping 9 -> 0.\n21\t- Otherwise `q` holds.\n22\t- `co` is a combinational signal that is high exactly when the *next* rising edge will\n23\t  perform a counting wrap from 9 to 0, i.e. `co = en && !load && (q == 9)`.\n24\t  It is low at all other times (in particular, it is low whenever `load` is high).\n25\t- `q` never holds a value above 9.\n26\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"067eba33-1a3a-4bb9-bdca-2fa0bc5ebb3b","uuid":"8db5cca3-3fda-4275-8d5e-04df707801fb","timestamp":"2026-10-19T23:42:54.059Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\abhig\\Documents\\New folder\\assay\\runs\\v1__mod10_counter__t3\\workspace\\spec.md","content":"# mod10_counter\n\nA 4-bit BCD (mod-10) up counter with synchronous load, count enable, and a carry-out.\n\n## Ports\n| Port  | Dir | Width | Description |\n|-------|-----|-------|-------------|\n| clk   | in  | 1     | Rising-edge clock |\n| rst_n | in  | 1     | Asynchronous active-low reset |\n| en    | in  | 1     | Count enable |\n| load  | in  | 1     | Synchronous load (has priority over `en`) |\n| d     | in  | 4     | Load value |\n| q     | out | 4     | Current count, 0..9 (registered) |\n| co    | out | 1     | Carry-out (combinational) |\n\n## Behavior\n- While `rst_n` is low, `q` is 0.\n- On a rising edge of `clk` with `load` high, `q` takes `d`. If `d` is greater than 9 (not a\n  valid BCD digit), `q` takes 0 instead. `load` works regardless of `en`.\n- Otherwise, on a rising edge with `en` high, `q` increments by 1, wrapping 9 -> 0.\n- Otherwise `q` holds.\n- `co` is a combinational signal that is high exactly when the *next* rising edge will\n  perform a counting wrap from 9 to 0, i.e. `co = en && !load && (q == 9)`.\n  It is low at all other times (in particular, it is low whenever `load` is high).\n- `q` never holds a value above 9.\n","numLines":26,"startLine":1,"totalLines":26}}}
